    "text": "Step 2: Use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of side $RT$. Since $\\sin{R} = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\frac{ST}{RT} = \\frac{2}{5}$, we can denote $ST = 2k$ and $RT = 5k$ for some positive constant $k$. The hypotenuse $RS$ is given as 5 units. Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n\\[ RT^2 = RS^2 - ST^2 \\]\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\n\\[ (5k)^2 = 5^2 - (2k)^2 \\]"
